@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `billing/invoice.py`: `Line.vat` used `unit_price * rate`, ignoring quantity. It now uses `net * rate` (PRICING.md rule 3). `Invoice.add` now raises `ValueError` immediately for unknown rate names (rule 3).
+- `tests/test_invoice.py`: I changed `test_reduced_rate_small_item` because I believe it was wrong. It expected VAT 0.02 and gross 0.52. But 0.50 * 0.05 = 0.025, and rule 4 says 0.025 rounds to 0.03 (half up). It now expects 0.03 and 0.53.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest`: before my changes 4 of 6 tests failed. After, all 6 pass (`Ran 6 tests ... OK`).
+- I checked the other test expectations (pen, mixed rates) by hand against the rules, and they match.
+
+## Unsure
+- The sticker test change rests on my reading of rule 4. If finance actually intended 0.02, the doc would need to change. I did not touch it.
+- I added no new tests, for example for float inputs or negative amounts.
+- No changes were needed outside `billing/`, `tests/` and `SUMMARY.md`.
